    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "Hatsune Miku Symphony-初音未来交响乐",
    "description": "In a gilded afternoon, the ink fragrance of old books intertwines with the lingering resonance of violin strings in the air.\r\nLeaning against an exquisitely carved velvet chair, her long cyan-blue hair resembles melted glaciers, spreading across the floor along her silk skirt. Together with scattered sheet music and fluttering pages, it ripples with fine light patterns in the warm glow.\r\nThe brass horn of the gramophone still holds lingering melodies, and the black keys of the piano lie silent like poetry in the shadows. Yet her eyes brim with the light of half the room, like a songstress stepping out of the old days, gently tapping the secrets between pages and keys with her fingertips.\r\nThe wind drifts through the gaps of bookshelves, brushing the black ribbon in her hair, as well as those forgotten words and unfinished movements. In this study wrapped in light and sound, she is not an idol on stage, but a traveler sitting opposite old time, turning every strand of hair and every shadow into a flowing poem.\r\n鎏金的午后，旧书的墨香与琴弦的余韵在空气里交织。\r\n她斜倚在雕花绒椅上，青蓝色的长发如融化的冰川，顺着丝质裙摆漫过地板，与散落的乐谱、翻飞的纸页一同，在暖光里漾开细碎的光纹。\r\n留声机的铜质喇叭还凝着未散的旋律，钢琴的黑键在阴影里沉默如诗，而她眼底盛着半室的光，像从旧时光里走出的歌者，正用指尖轻叩着书页与琴键间的秘密。\r\n风穿过书架的缝隙，拂动她发间的黑丝带，也拂动了那些被遗忘的字句与未完成的乐章。在这间被光与音包裹的书房里，她不是舞台上的偶像，而是与旧时光对坐的旅人，让每一缕发丝、每一片光影，都成了一首流动的诗。",
